/**
 * Harbour kitchen (港の食堂): make-to-order (put the dish together from the pantry to what the diner
 * says, or what the chef's recipe card / the menu board says: things and how many, the vessel,
 * fried / boiled / grilled, "no onions", allergies, substitutions, recipes) + sort & route (the
 * morning's delivery to the cold box / shelf / basket / freezer / bin, order tickets to the pan / pot /
 * grill, safety notices to the sink / stove / door / floor, customers' cards to thanks / ideas /
 * complaints). Domains: food, cooking, health, shopping.
 * Rank 1 ≈ 英検4級, 2 ≈ 3級, 3 ≈ 準2級, 4 ≈ 2級, 5 ≈ 準1級 (catering contracts, supplier complaints, inspection notes,
 * dietary menus, substitutes under conditions).
 *
 * Decipherability: the pantry always shows every ingredient with its picture and label, so a new food
 * noun is met next to its picture; methods and vessels are buttons with pictures; a wrong guess is
 * answered by the diner (the reaction names what was missing, extra or forbidden). Crates are read, not
 * looked at: a new label is placed by guessing and corrected by the boss (✗ and "this goes in …").
 * Grammar decides the answer: counts and "only / a few / more than / twice as many", "no / without /
 * not … but", "can't eat / allergic", "if there is no X, give Y", "children eat from bowls, adults from
 * plates", passive recipe cards ("must be boiled"), relative clauses ("the fish that is grilled").
 */
